WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.220
- All right, let's finish
up with something super fun

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:03.840
I found scrolling through social media.

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:05.001
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:05.001 --> 00:00:07.920
(rock music)

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:09.930
So sure, a charity can
straight up ask for money

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:10.860
to go to a good cause.

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:11.693
That's awesome.

00:00:11.693 --> 00:00:14.370
But one Minnesota organization
has gotten super creative

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:15.570
with their fundraising.

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:17.740
Every year they host a bed race.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:19.080
That's right.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.210
Hundreds of teams dress up in costumes

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:23.430
and ride mattresses down the tubing hill.

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:25.050
I love these people.

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:27.750
In the past 25 years, the
event has helped raise

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:30.330
more than 1 million to
provide those in need

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:32.670
with quality furniture
and household goods.

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:33.503
Super cool.

00:00:33.503 --> 00:00:35.970
We have the executive director
of Bridging on the line

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:38.700
watching on KSTP in Minneapolis.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:40.368
Let's say hi to Mark, everybody.

00:00:40.368 --> 00:00:41.970
(audience cheering)

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:42.810
- Hi Kelly.

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:43.890
- What's up, man?

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:45.690
So tell us about this annual bed race.

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:46.770
How crazy does it get?

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:48.090
Do people get crazy there?

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:49.620
- It gets super crazy.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:53.100
The annual Original Mattress
Factory Bed Race for Bridging

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:54.840
is a fabulous event.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:57.330
So, people gather in teams of four,

00:00:57.330 --> 00:01:01.860
they hop on a covered queen
size mattress in costume

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:04.200
like an inflatable unicorn

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:07.380
and then they raced down
a local snow tubing hill.

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:10.170
One year we had a team dressed as babies.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.900
They literally wore a sheet as a diaper.

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:16.950
We hope to have 100 teams
this year racing with us.

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:18.930
Ages will be 18 all the way up

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:20.580
to sometimes in their mid-seventies

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:24.120
people choose to join us
in this important cause.

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:26.430
And those beds that we race on, well,

00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:29.070
we give those to the families
whom we're privileged to serve

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:30.360
after the event.

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:32.550
So it is our 25th year.

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:34.740
It is on Saturday, March 11th,

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:37.350
and we hope to raise $125,000

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:39.600
to support our important cause.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:41.340
- Oh, that's incredible.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:44.160
Well, tell us more about Bridging.

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:46.320
- Yeah. We're a nonprofit furniture bank

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:48.750
and we get to work with
people who are transitioning

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:51.510
out of homelessness into stable housing,

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:53.940
and we get to provide them
with all the furniture

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:56.790
and household goods that are
gonna go into their new home.

00:01:56.790 --> 00:01:59.820
In fact, they get to select those items

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:01.680
at one of our two locations.

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:03.870
So they get to pick out their beds,

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:05.700
their kitchen tables and chairs,

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:07.290
their upholstered furniture.

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:09.150
They get to pick out their dishes,

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:10.410
their linens, their lamps,

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:11.940
all those things that are in our home

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:15.300
that we so often take for
granted they don't have.

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:18.900
And we get to provide that
for those amazing people.

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:22.315
In fact, we celebrate in
our 36 years of existence

00:02:22.315 --> 00:02:24.270
that we have been able to serve

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:29.270
more than 110,000 households
in our Twin Cities community.

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:32.850
We like to say we furnish homes with hope.

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:35.940
- Ah, that's so, that's incredible, man.

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:37.380
Thank you so much, Mark.

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:39.990
I'm loving your post right now, all right.

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:41.023
And that's not all.

00:02:41.023 --> 00:02:42.090
- I really appreciate that Kelly.

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:43.080
Thanks so much.

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:44.970
- Oh, that, well, no, we're not done.

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:45.803
That's not all.

00:02:45.803 --> 00:02:47.670
Our season long partner
Pilot Pen makers of G2,

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:49.650
the go-to pen of "The Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:51.780
want to honor truly unstoppable people,

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:53.580
just like the people in the race

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:55.260
and people like you who serve,

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:57.780
so they're gonna be writing
Bridging a check for $1,000.

00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:59.276
How's that sound?

00:02:59.276 --> 00:03:01.500
- Hey, thank you so much.

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:02.340
That is awesome.

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:05.040
We're on our way to $125,000 goal.

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:06.000
Thank you, thank you.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:06.930
- Aw, awesome.

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:08.714
Thank you so much, mark.

00:03:08.714 --> 00:03:10.200
And thank you to all our guests this hour,

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:12.660
Rose Byrne, Harry Hamlin, Rochelle,

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:14.730
Sean Adam, Lucas Graham, and Micky Guidan.

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:15.563
Y'all have a great day,

00:03:15.563 --> 00:03:18.487
and if it's not, try and change it.

